# Oblivious Bookworm: "a permanent entered the battlefield face down under your control". On Bot1's turn 3 Bot2 manifests
# dread at instant speed - Turn Inside Out on its own Llanowar Elves, then Lightning Bolt on them, off Black Lotus - so a
# permanent entered face down this turn, but under Bot2's control: Bot1's end-step draw is still followed by a discard.
#
# Bot1 casts the Bookworm on turn 1 and declines that end step's draw; on turn 3 it accepts, draws Counterspell and
# discards it. Bot2's Snapcaster Mage is face down on its battlefield at the end.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Oblivious Bookworm
Island x4
Island
Counterspell
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Llanowar Elves
Turn Inside Out
Lightning Bolt
Swamp x2
Swamp
Snapcaster Mage
Swamp x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oblivious Bookworm.Cast
[T1 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Decline
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Turn Inside Out.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Arrange(Snapcaster Mage | Swamp)
? Bot2.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Choose(Counterspell)

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
Bot1.Library.Count = 10
Bot1.Graveyard = Counterspell
Bot2.Battlefield..FaceDownName = Snapcaster Mage
